{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED at exact clean head 1e8d3fd82c12977b245ffca8f17056f2ebd63edb, artifact 199c247546c75c166c3cb482b3431ce0e850385b.\n\nThe three prior blockers are closed.\n\n1. Clause admission now receives the fold's ruling and refuses a clause-shaped statement unless its decision is effective. Projection.Statements remains an audit of what was said; it is no longer mistaken for force.\n\n2. The selected charter must be present in the clause's direct signed bases. underCharter uses slices.Contains(source.Bases, charter); it does not walk transitive ancestry or invent delegation from an intermediate rests_on edge.\n\n3. The command-level test exercises the composed path from Workroom Projection.Decisions and Projection.Provenance through clauseSources and authors into ClausesFrom. It proves an effective direct-basis clause admits, an ineffective clause is refused, a clause under another charter is refused, and an empty selected charter admits nothing.\n\nThe merge resolution is correct. residentclient.ResolveActor produces actorName before authorization. The command independently selects observe or propose, then passes both actorName and operation to charterIsLive. The same actorName is used later to load the signing key and build an observation. An environment-resolved identity therefore cannot be authorized as the empty flag value, and an observation-only charter cannot acquire propose authority. The exact head is current with main and cleanly mergeable.\n\nArchitecture: affected layers are the Workroom application profile/projection boundary and the GitHub connector/CLI surface, with the shared resident-client surface supplying resolved identity. The semantic-free kernel, Nexus, interpreter, and projection contracts do not change. The exact head preserves docs/reference/architecture.md; no architecture-page change or re-anchoring is required.\n\nSecurity: the changed admission and forge-write boundaries fail closed on ineffective, foreign-charter, stale, retired, wrong-actor, wrong-repository, and unauthorized-operation inputs. Request/artifact/head coherence remains checked before the irreversible POST, and inbound issue bodies remain data rather than authority. I found no unresolved security defect introduced or exposed by this exact delta. The separately filed pre-existing observation-suppression request #2950 remains outside this correction and should keep its own review chain. I performed no public GitHub side effect.\n\nSimplification: the direct-basis slice membership and one decision map are already simpler than the prior ancestry walk and do not warrant replacement. One nonblocking cleanup remains in TestTheCommandAdmitsOnlyEffectiveClausesCitingTheSelectedCharter: its local clause helper accepts an unused basis argument; removing that parameter would express the fixture more plainly but does not weaken or obscure the proof.\n\nVerification at this exact head: focused connector tests passed three times; focused race and vet passed; make test, make vet, make docs, make build, and git diff --check passed. The worktree stayed clean.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:199c247546c75c166c3cb482b3431ce0e850385b","head":"1e8d3fd82c12977b245ffca8f17056f2ebd63edb","verdict":"approved"}}